/home/sat/mcrl-hub/dr9-prompts/PROMPT-9C-energy-model-realism.md:2:You are a satellite payload and link-budget specialist. The attached note gives the successor model's equations and a worked angle → power → EE table; the regime and synthetic reports give operating points. Model summary: per-user rate target r* = 50 Mbit/s; the lowest ACM mode from EN 302 307-1 Table 13 that meets the target under equal-airtime TDM with n_b users per beam; required RF power p_u = min(1.65 W, Γ_r·(N₀W + Î)/ĥ) solved as a coupled capped fixed point across beams; PA supply power √(p·p_sat)/0.35 with p_sat = 5.218 W evaluated per slot and averaged over airtime; 0.338 W per active beam chain; 0.200 W per active satellite; optional idle power 1/12 of PA supply at cap; bits and joules integrated over 47 sub-intervals of a 30.08 s step; service = SINR ≥ the mode threshold after joint resolution.
