     2	
     3	# PROVFIX — provisioning decision, closed 2026-09-10
     4	
     5	## Disposition
     6	
     7	The sealed provisioning rule is delivering the convention its declarations specify. It provisions executed and predicted power from nominal gains, then applies the pre-specified tenth-percentile wanted-link quantile only in the mode/service selection view. The resulting transmitted mode may be below the rate-target mode or absent. That consequence is severe, but it is not a failure of a declared guaranteed-rate service because no such service was declared.
     8	
     9	Accordingly, no provisioning policy change is authorised, no declaration is superseded, and no affected-comparison rerun is required. The observation **0 of 2,000 rate targets attained is not a breach**. PROVFIX is closed; changing the planning objective later would require a new, prospectively declared versioned amendment rather than reopening this item as defect correction.
    10	
    11	This disposition is based on the declared contract and its precedence, not on whether either provisioning convention improves any route's sign, any energy-efficiency figure, or any preferred result.
    12	
    13	## Verified against files opened
    14	
    15	### The governing declarations
    16	
    17	I read the base declaration and every amendment/erratum from v1.1 through v1.9 in full before forming this view.
