    22	
    23	Source: [base priority declaration, line 14](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:14).
    24	
    25	The v1.1 amendment defines the target and accounting as follows:
    26	
    27	> “**Primary architecture: (a-r) `V025-ANGLE-RATE-TPC-TDM-ACM`** — memoryless angle-aware power control with a per-user nominal rate target r* = 50 000 000 bit/s (inherited as a synthetic operating point from Track B lever L1; explicitly not calibrated demand).”
    28	
    29	> “**Infeasibility / accounting:** if no MODCOD meets the rate at the cap, mark the target infeasible and transmit at the RF cap; keep actual partial delivery, interference and energy; no pruning or repacking. PHY service (decodability) is unchanged; rate-target attainment is reported separately. Bits = achieved decodable ACM bits (full buffer).”
    30	
    31	Source: [v1.1 amendment, lines 6–7](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6).
    32	
    33	The v1.7 erratum withdraws an availability interpretation and declares a scoring convention instead:
    34	
    35	> “The margin rationale is renamed, not re-justified. v1.6 §1 called the q₁₀ level ‘the standard 90 %-availability link-budget convention’. That is withdrawn: a per-link 10th-percentile channel-gain quantile does not establish 90 % network availability, and no such universal convention is claimed. The rule is named exactly what it is: a **pre-specified tenth-percentile channel-gain scoring rule**, applied identically to every arm, with the level fixed before any formal outcome and disclosed as having followed development inspection. Its diagnostic sensitivity at q₀₅/q₂₅ stands.”
    36	
    37	Source: [v1.7 erratum, §1](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.7-ERRATUM-2026-09-09.md:5).
    38	
    39	The v1.8 amendment makes the numerator and setpoint semantics explicit:
    40	
    41	> “**Traffic model declared explicitly.** The numerator is saturated (full-buffer) decodable throughput under a per-user rate-target power controller; the rate target is a **power-control setpoint, not a demand model**, and realised per-user rates may exceed it. Reported alongside every claim: rate attainment, availability and the coverage/outage distribution. Finite demand or queues would be a versioned model amendment with affected comparisons re-run, never a relabelling.”
    42	
    43	Source: [v1.8 amendment, §5](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.8-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9).
    44	
