/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:27:The original 22.99× cancellation argument is unavailable. The opened worker audit derives a mixed-path residual offset `(size−1) × epsilon` and places the alleged cancellation inside its sampled artifact envelope; it explicitly says a corrected decomposition is not determined (`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/PATH-ARTEFACT-CHECKS-2026-09-10.md:11–36`). The feasibility erratum acknowledges this (`C/V025-CONTROLLER-FEASIBILITY-2026-09-10.md:110–126`). An envelope overlap invalidates that particular inference; it does not prove all physical cancellation disappears. **UNDETERMINED:** actual conditioning and achievable decision regret on the repaired, path-consistent target. Settling them requires corresponding labeled receipts and held-out decisions, followed by the specified EE comparison.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:61:**Derived.** A conjunction can be tested by an intersection–union test without a Bonferroni correction when the sole claim requires every component: under the union null, at least one component null is true, and conjunction rejection requires rejecting it. This assumes valid component tests. Conjunction **power**, however, depends on the joint distribution of all effects and errors. Multiplying six marginal powers requires independence, which shared FULL/control arms do not establish. The three-contrast calibration cannot supply six-contrast power by assertion. **UNDETERMINED:** the final standalone comparator, applicable margins, and calibrated six-contrast power. A reconciled estimand specification and matched joint calibration would settle these.
