/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/ADJUDICATION-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:101:The ~+400% attribution also needs restraint. The opened smoke verifies **FULL versus external BASELINE = +401.714321%**, not an isolated head-independent argmax effect. Its inspected proposal-repair code ranks legal profiles by learned Q1+Q2 (`R/scripts/run_c3_panel_smoke.py:395–400`; `R/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:512–546`). Equal repaired seeds do not prove that this computation is head-independent. **UNDETERMINED:** the controller's particular +400% attribution to a separate exact-surplus one-shot step. A matching receipt with carrier, exact one-shot and learned endpoints, together with authenticated executable provenance, would settle it. The carrier comparison cannot establish route ownership in any event.
