/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:107:**A. “The exact path repairs the data while preserving the inputs needed by a cheap predictor.” Wrong. V-code/V-receipt.** The [exact builder, lines 599–672][exactinputs] fills Q1 features from the candidate's evaluated margin, required power and ACM efficiency; Q2 features include evaluated future projections. [The cost receipt][rowcost] identifies those suppliers explicitly. The [data census][census] finds all Q1 and Q2 state vectors differ across the two paths at both diffed anchors. Switching paths changes features as well as labels, despite retaining the same dimensional schema. Some feature acquisition requires the very candidate solve the head is supposed to avoid. That may be allowed in an offline teacher; it is not free inference. The deployment feature supplier and its cost remain **UNDETERMINED** for the proposed successor.
