/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:183:Failure of all tested estimators leaves the architectural-versus-informational cause **UNDETERMINED** unless there is additional identification evidence. Exact same-input/different-target cases prove ambiguity for those cases; quantify their mass and whether they reverse relevant decisions. Absence of observed collisions does not prove sufficiency. A model that succeeds only after reading coupled candidate outcomes establishes an oracle-feature result. Under no outcome should R², loss or ordering be restated as an EE gain. Under no outcome does target predictability alone prove the benefit of informative-source training.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:187:Report row inclusion and coalition coverage, including empty/singleton handling, grand rows and missing sizes; legality filtering can change the training population. Separate target generation from inference-feature acquisition. For cost reconciliation, equal row counts do not imply equal work. If 49.03 and 632.83 seconds are reconciled by boundary count, optional coalition work or execution settings, state that mechanism and scope the rate accordingly. If not, cost is **UNDETERMINED**, not “affordable because one receipt says so.” Partial completion is an exact partial corpus, not a completed corpus. A complete corpus is readiness evidence, never EE evidence.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-strategic-astra-ws/SWEEP-ASTRA-2026-09-10.md:201:Finally, a positive exact factorial does **not** pass a learned-source claim or demonstrate learnability. Under the owner's revised goal, report magnitudes without inventing a numerical “substantial” threshold after seeing them. If no prospective practical threshold exists, the mechanical G1 pass/fail is **UNDETERMINED** and the result is a planning input. This is a limit on the conclusion, not a reason to commission another open-ended audit cycle.
